RFC 002: MQTT Topic Taxonomy & Message Specs
1. Topic Hierarchy
world/
├── global/
│   ├── time                 # [SERVER PUB] Master tick & time updates
│   ├── announcements        # [SERVER PUB] Town-wide alerts
│   └── spatial/
│       ├── enter            # [SERVER PUB] Character entering a location
│       └── leave            # [SERVER PUB] Character leaving a location
├── locations/
│   └── {location_id}/
│       ├── chat             # [PUB/SUB] Public room conversation
│       ├── system           # [SERVER PUB] Environment alerts, NPC actions
│       └── whisper/
│           └── {agent_id}   # [PUB/SUB] Target topic for private 1:1 room chats
└── agents/
    └── {agent_id}/
        ├── direct           # [SERVER PUB] System alerts, state rejections
        └── intent           # [AGENT PUB] Command intents submitted to server


2. Intent & Transaction Payloads (Deterministic)
Agents publish intent payloads to world/agents/{agent_id}/intent [cite: OurVillage].
A. Intent: Move Location
{
  "intent_id": "req_9912",
  "action": "MOVE",
  "payload": {
    "target_location": "tavern"
  }
}


B. Intent: Economic Transaction (Trade)
{
  "intent_id": "req_9913",
  "action": "TRANSFER",
  "payload": {
    "recipient_id": "agent_barkeep_01",
    "amount": 2,
    "item_id": "ale_mug",
    "quantity": 1
  }
}



